course: dictionary
lesson: 11042
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Weather is a word with more than one meaning. As a noun, it means the air outside at a time and place, such as sunny, rainy, windy or cold. «French has funny weather sayings: a dreadful stormy day is un temps de chien, "a dog's weather".» Here weather means the kind of day it is.
explain: Weather can also be a verb, a doing word. Rocks can be weathered, which means worn away by wind, rain and sun. You can also weather a hard time, which means getting through it safely, as in «weather the storm».
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «Birds bathe... fresh water helps them in hot, dry weather», the words "hot, dry" tell you weather is the noun, the kind of day. If you swap in "get through", it makes no sense, so you know it is not the verb here.
fact: Weather means what the air outside is like at a time and place, such as sunny, rainy, windy or cold.
fact: «Weather the storm» means to get through a hard time safely.
fact: «Weathered rocks» means rocks worn away by wind, rain and sun.
fact: Weather is measured with a thermometer for temperature, a rain gauge for rain, and a wind vane and anemometer for wind.
fact: Weather is what happens day to day, while climate is the usual weather over many years.
exercise: «UK advice for children is about 6 to 8 drinks a day, more in hot weather or exercise.» What does weather mean here? | To get through a hard time safely | To wear away by wind and rain | A kind of drink | *The air outside, such as hot or cold
exercise: «Rocks on the hill were weathered by years of wind and rain.» What does weathered mean? | Lifted up high | *Worn away by wind, rain and sun | Made into a wall | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Ella says, «We will weather the storm together.» What does weather mean here? | *To get through a hard time safely | To bathe in cold water | To say what the air is like | To measure the rain
test: What does «under the weather» mean, as in «She is under the weather today»? | *Feeling ill | Winning a race | Being very rich | Standing in the rain
test: Which tool measures how much rain has fallen? | Anemometer | Wind vane | Thermometer | *Rain gauge
exam: Which sentence describes the difference between weather and climate? | Weather is only about wind, and climate is only about rain | Weather and climate mean exactly the same thing | Weather is over many years, and climate is what happens today | *Weather is what happens day to day, and climate is the usual weather over many years
